hadiths[80]{hadithnumber,text}:
"684","Shaqiq narrates: Once I was sitting with Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud and Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with them). Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said: ""O Abu Abd al-Rahman! What do you think if a person who becomes janib does not get water for a month, he will continue to perform tayammum during that time?"" So Sayyiduna Abdullah said: ""He will not perform Tayammum, even if he does not get water for a month."" So Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari said: ""Then what will you say about this verse? Which is present in Surah Al-Maida (God's guidance) 'then you do not find water, then perform tayammum through pure soil'."" Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu said: ""If people are given permission in this regard, a time will soon come when they will find the water cold, so they will start doing tayammum with pure mud."" The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Musa asked him: ""You dislike him for this reason?"" He replied: ""Yes."" So Sayyidna Abu Musa said to him: ""Didn't you hear what Ammar said to Sayyidna Umar?"" (He narrated): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on some errand. I got sidetracked, I didn't get water. I collapsed into the mud like an animal. Then I attended the service of the Holy Prophet. When I mentioned this to him, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It was enough for you that you would wipe both hands on the ground with one of them and then wipe your face with both of them."" So Sayyidna Abdullah replied: ""You did not think about Sayyidna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu, Sayyidna Umar was not satisfied with the statement of Sayyidna Ammar Radi Allahu Anhu."" The words of a narrator named Yusuf are: ""You wipe both your hands on the ground, then wipe your face and both arms with them."" Sayyidna Abdullah said: ""Have you not seen this? Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did not content himself with the statement of Sayyidna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"685","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He (may God bless him and grant him peace) said: ""There are two strokes in Tayammum. One stroke is for the face and one stroke is for both arms up to the elbows."" A narrator named Ali bin Zabayan has narrated it as a marfu' tradition which other men have narrated as muwaqf and this is correct."
"686","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""There are two strokes in Tayammum. One stroke is for the face and one stroke is for both arms up to the elbows (for wiping)."""
"687","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to perform Tayammum up to his elbows."
"688","Salim narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): We performed tayammum with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, during his time in al-Aqdas. We used to strike our hands on clean clay and then we would wipe our hands and then wipe our face with it."
"689","Salim narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): We performed tayammum with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (i.e. in his time). It consists of two multiplications. One stroke was for the face and both palms, while one stroke was for both arms up to the elbows. The two narrators of this tradition are Sulaiman bin Arqam and Sulaiman bin Abu Dawud."
"690","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about tayammum: ""There will be two strokes. One stroke will be for the face, and the other stroke will be for the hands up to the elbows."""
"691","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""One stroke in tayammum is for the face and one stroke is for the wrists to the elbows."" All its narrators are reliable, but the truth is that this tradition is suspended."
"692","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that a person came and said: ""Janabat has come upon me. I have become spoiled in the mud."" So he said: ""Strike (your hands) on the ground."" So he struck his hand on the ground and wiped his face with both hands, then he struck his other hand on the ground and wiped his hands up to the elbows with it."
"693","A narrator named Aban narrates: Qatadah was asked about tayammum during the journey, and he replied, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) used to say that it would be done up to the elbows. Hasan al-Basri and Ibrahim Nakhai say: Up to the elbows (will be wiped). Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrated this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Tayammum will be performed up to the elbows."" A narrator named Abu Ishaq narrates: I mentioned this tradition to Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal and he liked this tradition very much. He said: ""What a wonderful tradition."""
"694","Salim narrates this about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: When he performed tayammum, he used to strike both hands on the ground. Through them, they used to wipe their hands up to both elbows. They did not sweep the soil with their hands."
"695","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: ""(In tayammum) there will be two strokes. One stroke will be for the face and one stroke will be for both arms."""
"696","Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to perform Tayammum on his face and both arms."
"697","Sayyiduna Ammar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Tayammum is the name of striking (i.e. wiping over) the face and both arms."""
"698","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (may God be pleased with him) that a person came and said: ""I have been afflicted with janabat and I have become spoiled in the dust."" So they said: ""Strike your hands on the ground."" He struck his hand on the ground and then wiped his face with it and then again struck his hand on the ground and then wiped both his arms up to the elbows with these two hands."
"699","Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""There is only one stroke in Tayammum, which is for the face and both arms."" A narrator named Ramadi narrates: A narrator named Yazid narrates: Whoever adopts this hadith, there is nothing wrong with it."
"700","Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""That much is enough for you."" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his hand on the blessed earth, then he blew on it and wiped his face and both arms with it."
"701","Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrates: Once he got sidetracked during a journey and fell into the mud. When he came to the Prophet (PBUH) and told him about it, the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""O Ammar! It would have been enough for you to strike your two hands on the dirt, then blow on them, then rub your hands with them up to your face and wrists."" This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Ibrahim as a superior tradition, while other narrators have narrated it as a fixed tradition, and its narrator Abu Malik is considered to have hadiths from Sayyidna Ammar, because other narrators have narrated it from Sayyidna Ammar, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding this Abu Malik."
"702","A narrator named Abu Malik narrates: I heard Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir giving a sermon in Kufa, and he mentioned Tayammum and said: ""In it one will strike one's hand on the ground and wipe one's face and both arms with it."""
"703","Abu Malik narrates this about Sayyidna Ammar: He struck his palms on the clay and blew on it and spread it on his face and wiped both arms up to the joints, then Sayyidna Ammar said: ""Tayammum is done like this."" This same tradition is narrated as a hadith along with another chain of narrators on the authority of Sayyidna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"704","Imam al-Shaabi states: It is necessary to perform tayammum on the part which is ordered to be washed. The organ which is not ordered to be washed will be abandoned in Tayammum."
"705","Imam Sha'bi states: We have been ordered to perform tayammum on those parts of ourselves which have been ordered to be washed (in ablution)."
"706","Qatadah narrates: Sayyiduna Amr bin As used to perform tayammum for every prayer. Qatadah himself used to issue fatwas accordingly."
"707","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""Tayammum will be performed for every prayer."""
"708","Sayyiduna Amr bin As says: ""Tayammum will be performed for every prayer."""
"709","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar used to perform tayammum for every prayer."
"710","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: ""This is a Sunnah, a person should pray only one prayer with Tayammum and then perform Tayammum (again) for the second prayer."" The narrator of this hadith is Hasan bin Amara."
"711","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: ""It is a Sunnah that a man should not offer more than one prayer with one Tayammum."""
"712","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: ""Only one prayer will be performed through Tayammum."""
"713","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A person who performs tayammum should not lead those who perform ablution."" Its evidence is weak."
"714","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""A bound person should not lead the absolute people and a person performing tayammum should not lead those who perform ablution."""
"715","The same tradition about Tayammum is narrated along with another chain of transmission."
"716","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing tayammum at a place called Murbad-ul-Naam, while he (peace be upon him) was observing the houses of Madinah from this place."""
"717","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to perform tayammum at Murbad al-Naam, which is three miles away from Madinah Munawwarah."
"718","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"719","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) performed tayammum at a distance of one or two miles from Madinah and offered Asr prayer, then he came to (the city) and the sun was still high. He did not pray again."
"720","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""When a person is on a journey, he should calculate the time between himself and the last time of prayer. If he cannot find water, he should perform tayammum."""
"721","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Pure soil is a means of ablution for a Muslim, even if he does not get water for ten years."""
"722","Abu Qalaba narrates this regarding a person from Banu Amir: I was told about Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, so I attended his service. I asked him: ""Are you Sayyidna Abu Dharr?"" He replied: ""That's what my family calls me."" Then Sayyidna Abu Dharr Ghafari Radiyallahu Anhu said: Once I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have become a victim of death."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What has caused you to perish?"" I said: ""I was in a place where no water could be found. I had my wife with me. I got janabat."" So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Pure soil is a means of attaining purity until a man finds water, even if ten years pass. When you find water, pour it on your body."""
"723","Mahlab narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari Radiyallahu Anhu: He said: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet PBUH and the Prophet PBUH said: ""O Abu Dharr! Indeed, mud is a means of purification for a person who does not get water, even if he does not get it for ten years. When you find water, pour it on your body."""
"724","Amr bin Bajdan narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari quoting the Prophet sallallahu alaihi wa sallam saying: ""Indeed, pure soil is a means of purification for a Muslim if it lasts for ten years. When a man drinks water, he should pour water over his body. It will be better for him."""
"725","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Dharr Ghafari, may Allah be pleased with him, but it contains these words: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: ""This is a means of attaining purity."""
"726","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Pure soil is a means of attaining purity, even if a person does not get water for ten years. When you drink water, pour it over your skin."" A narrator named Raja bin Aamir has narrated it in this way, but it is true that it is related to a person belonging to Banu Amir, as Ibn Alayhi narrated it from a narrator named Ibn Ayyub."
"727","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once two men set out on a journey. It was time for prayer in front of both of them. They didn't have water, they both performed tayammum through pure clay then during this prayer time they both got water. One of them performed ablution and offered the prayer again, while the other person did not offer the prayer again. Then these two came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned this to him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the person who had not repeated the prayer: ""You have done well, your prayer has been correct."" To the other person who performed ablution and prayed again, he said: ""You will have a double reward."" In narrating this tradition through a narrator named Layth, the narrator named Abdullah ibn Nafi is unique. Ibn Mubarak and other Muhadditheen have narrated a tradition to the contrary."
"728","On the authority of Abdullah bin Mubarak, Ata bin Yasar narrates: Both of these men were given janabat. Both of them performed Tayammum, Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) is not mentioned in this hadith."
"729","Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Once we set out on a journey. One of us was hit by a stone which injured his head and then he got concussion. He inquired of his companions: ""Do you think I need to perform tayammum?"" The Companions replied: ""When you are able to use water, there is no leave for you with us."" The person took a bath and died. We came to the service of the Holy Prophet. When you were told about it, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These people killed him. May Allah destroy them. Why did they not inquire when they did not know, the healing of a sick person in questioning. It was enough for that person that he would perform tayammum (bandage) and (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words) bandage his wound and anoint it and wash the rest of his body."" The narrator named Musa is in doubt here. Shaykh Abu Bakr states: The people of Makkah are unique in narrating this tradition and the people of Al-Jazira transmitted it. He has not narrated it from Sayyidina Jabir regarding Ata. This tradition is only narrated by a narrator named Zubair and is not authentic. Imam Uza'i has narrated a hadith to the contrary, which is narrated from Sayyidna Abdullah regarding Ata. There is also a difference of opinion in quoting from Imam Uza'i. According to one tradition, it was narrated from Ata, and according to another tradition, it was narrated from him: ""I have come to know this regarding Ata."" And Imam Uza'i has quoted the last part of it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Ata as a transmitted tradition, and this is correct. Ibn Abi Hatim narrates: I asked my father and a narrator named Shaykh Abi Zariyah about it, and they both replied: This hadith was narrated by Ibn al-Ashireen, on the authority of Uza'i, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him. These gentlemen have quoted it as an authentic tradition."
"730","Ata narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrated this: A person was wounded during the time of the Holy Prophet (SAW). He was embarrassed. When he discovered the problem, he was told that he had to take a ghusl, which he did and died. When the Prophet (PBUH) was informed about this, he (PBUH) said: ""These people have killed him. May Allah destroy them. Isn't the healing of a sick person in questioning?"""
"731","A narrator named Ata narrates that he came to know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about this, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if the person had washed his body and left the head where the wound was, it would have been permissible for him to do so. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"732","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA)."
"733","Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates that he heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas narrating that during the time of the Holy Prophet, a man was injured, then he developed a fever, so he was asked to take a bath. He took bath and died. When this was reported to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said that those people killed him. May Allah destroy these people, isn't the healing of a sick person in questioning? A narrator named Ata narrates that we came to know that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if the person had washed his body and left the part of his head where the wound was, it would have been correct."
"734","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"735","This same hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) along with another chain of transmission."
"736","The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) along with another chain of transmission, while other narrators have also followed it."
"737","Sayyiduna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution, then he (PBUH) wiped his forehead, turban and both socks."
"738","The sons of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate on the authority of their father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) anointed both his socks, the front of his head and his turban."
"739","The sons of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrated the same thing from the Prophet (PBUH) regarding his father. A narrator has narrated these words in his hadith that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped the front of his head, the front of his forehead, his two socks and his cloak."
"740","The sons of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrate on the authority of their father that the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution. You wiped your forehead, wiped both socks and wiped your turban. A narrator named Bakr has narrated that I heard this hadith from the son of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba."
"741","A narrator named Hammam narrates that Sayyiduna Jarir (may God be pleased with him) urinated, then wiped his socks while performing ablution. So they were asked why you have done this, you have already urinated? He replied, ""I saw the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, first he urinated, then after that he performed ablution and wiped both socks."" A narrator named Amish narrates that Ibrahim says that these people liked this hadeeth very much, the reason being that Sayyiduna Jarir (RA) accepted Islam after Surah Maida was revealed. A narrator named Isa bin Yunus narrated in his tradition that he was asked, ""O Abu Amr! You are doing this, have you urinated before?"" So he replied that what would prevent me from doing that when I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping his socks. The disciples of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) liked this tradition very much because Sayyidna Jarir (RA) accepted Islam after the revelation of Surah Maida."
"742","Hammam bin Harith narrates that I saw Sayyiduna Jarir, may God be pleased with him, he performed ablution with the ablution vessel and then wiped his socks. He was asked if you are wiping your socks? So he replied that I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping his socks. This tradition was very liked by the students of Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him). He used to say that Sayyiduna Jarir (RA) accepted Islam after Surah Maida was revealed."
"743","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"744","Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah Bijli (RA) narrates that I came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) after the revelation of Surah al-Maidah. I saw you wipe your socks."
"745","Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping his socks. People inquired whether you saw this after Surah al-Maida was revealed. He said that I accepted Islam after Surah Maida was revealed."
"746","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that after Surah Maida was revealed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued to wipe his socks until he appeared in the presence of Allah."
"747","Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra (RA) narrates from the Prophet (PBUH) on the authority of his father that he allowed a traveler to wipe his feet for three days and three nights, while a resident for one day and one night. If a man wears socks after performing ablution, he can wipe the socks during that time. A narrator named Abu Ash'ath states that a traveler can wipe it for three days and three nights while a resident can wipe it for one day and one night."
"748","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"749","Urwa bin Mughirah narrates on the authority of his father that I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace! Are you wiping your socks?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I wore both of them in such a state that they were both clean."
"750","Sayyiduna Hasan Basri states that the upper part of the socks will be wiped, like lines will be made with the fingers."
"751","This tradition is also narrated along with a document."
"752","Sayyiduna Al-Mughira (RA) says: I performed ablution on the Prophet (PBUH) on the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk, so he wiped the upper part and the lower part of the socks."
"753","The same hadith is transmitted as Mursal Hadith along with another chain of transmission, in which Sayyiduna Mughirah (RA) was not mentioned."
"754","Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates that I saw the Prophet (PBUH) wiping the top of his socks."
"755","Salim narrates on the authority of his father Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that Sayyidna Sa’d (RA) inquired from Sayyidna Umar (RA) about wiping the socks, and he said, “I heard the Prophet (PBUH) commanding to wipe the upper part of the socks, which is three days and three nights for a traveler and one day and one night for a resident."
"756","Mufadl bin Fazalah narrates that I asked Yazid bin Abu Habib about wiping over the socks, and he said that Abdullah bin Huqam has quoted this statement of Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may God be pleased with him) with reference to Ali bin Rabah. Sayyiduna Uqbah told him that once he joined a delegation and attended the service of Sayyiduna Umar. Uqba says that at that time I was wearing thick socks and that day was Friday. So Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said to them that you have acted according to the Sunnah. One hadith has the words that you have done right, but the word ""Sunnah"" is not mentioned in it."
"757","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I left Syria on Friday to go to Madinah and reached Madinah on Friday. I attended the service of Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu, and he asked, ""How long have you been wearing socks on your feet?"" I replied that last Friday. They inquired whether you had taken them off. I replied that no! So he said that you have acted according to the Sunnah. Sheikh Abu Bakr says that this hadith is poor. Sheikh Abul Hasan says that its chain of transmission is authentic."
"758","Nafi' narrated that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did not set a time limit for wiping over the socks."
"759","Nafi', narrates about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he says that there is no time limit for wiping the socks, you wipe them until you take them off."
"760","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the traveler used to wipe his socks until he took them off."
"761","Zar bin Habish narrates that I attended the service of Sayyidna Safwan bin Asal. He asked why you came? I replied that I have come to acquire knowledge. So he said, ""I heard the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that whoever leaves his home to seek knowledge, the angels are pleased with his action and rest on him."" Zar said, ""I have come to inquire about wiping on the socks."" So he replied that I was among the army that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent on a campaign and instructed us that you can wipe your socks for three days during the journey and for one day and one night during the stay, while we have worn them in a state of ablution and we will not take them off while urinating, defecating or getting up after sleeping, we will only take them off in a state of Janabat. Sayyiduna Safwan (RA) also said that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that there is a door in the West that is open for repentance, the width of which is the distance of seventy years. It will not close until the sun rises from its side."
"762","Ali bin Ibrahim narrates that I heard Shaykh Abu Bakr bin Khuzima saying that I mentioned the tradition of Abdul Razzaq to Imam Muzni, so he said to me that our companions have also narrated this tradition, because Imam Shafi'i has no other authentic argument than this. The author says that these words of the hadeeth that when we entered them in the state of ablution."
"763","``Urwa bin Mughirah narrates the statement of his father that I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him! Can any of us wipe his socks?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when this person has entered them both in a state of ablution."
